[38;5;231m⏺[39m This one hits a security-posture consequence beyond the line itself, so I want your explicit go-ahead before editing.

  [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m is [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m, and [38;5;153mserver.js:3[39m confirms it governs session expiry. Going to 8 hours (480)
  means a 16× longer window in which a stolen session token, an unattended logged-in browser, or a hijacked session
  stays valid — and a revoked or deprovisioned user keeps access for up to 8 hours instead of 30 minutes. That's a real
  change to the app's blast radius, not just a number.

